#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# polynomial_mod

#% text
# `polynomial_mod(p, m)` reduces the coefficients of p modulo the integer m, or gives the remainder of p on division by the polynomial m.

#% text
# `polynomial_mod(p, [m1, m2, ...])` reduces by each modulus in turn.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A rational coefficient a/b is reduced to a b^-1 mod m when b is invertible modulo m. A polynomial modulus is divided in its first variable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
polynomial_mod(3*x^2 + 2*x + 1, 2)
#% output
#= 1 + x^2

#% cell
polynomial_mod(3*x^2 + 2*x + 1, x^2 + 1)
#% output
#= -2 + 2*x

#% cell
polynomial_mod(3*x^3 + 21*x^2 - 7*x + 55, [2*x^2 - 7, 9])
#% output
#= 7 + 8*x

#% text
# With several variables the remainder is that of the multivariate division in the lexicographic order of the sorted variables, so it is a polynomial (`x^2 y` modulo `x y - 1` is `x`, not `1/y`):

#% cell
polynomial_mod(x^2*y, x*y - 1)
#% output
#= x

#% cell
polynomial_mod(x^2 + a^2, a*x - 1)
#% output
#= a^2 + x^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `polynomial_remainder`, `mod`, `polynomial_reduce`
